Trace the retry counter below and implement `traceAttemptCount()` to return the exact stdout. The routine records each frame when it begins, marks the base case, and records each frame again after its child returns. Explain the order in which the calls and returns appear.

```js
function visit(remaining, events) {
  events.push('enter:' + remaining);
  if (remaining === 0) {
    events.push('base');
    return;
  }
  visit(remaining - 1, events);
  events.push('leave:' + remaining);
}
const events = [];
visit(2, events);
console.log(events.join('|'));
```

**Requirements:**
- Return one fresh string array containing the exact stdout line.
- Recreate the recursive event order rather than hardcoding the observed output.
- Simulate the calls with an explicit stack of frame records; do not call the recursive snippet directly. Each frame needs an entry or return phase.
- Explain which frame returns first and when its caller resumes.

**Return Contract:**
- Return `string[]` with exact event order and separators.

