Trace the bounded retry scheduler below and implement `traceRetrySchedule()` to return the exact stdout. The policy allows three attempts. Explain whether the stopping boundary preserves that contract.

```js
function retrySchedule(remaining) {
  if (remaining <= 1) return ['stop'];
  return ['try-' + remaining, ...retrySchedule(remaining - 1)];
}
console.log(retrySchedule(3).join('>'));
```

**Requirements:**
- Return a fresh array containing the exact stdout line produced by this code.
- Recreate the recursive logic; do not hardcode the observed line.
